{"id":"e4bf948cdb19013b","group":"58","path":"58/batch11/58-df-seiberg-witten.md","title":"Zero-Dimensional Seiberg–Witten Invariant","display":"df-seiberg-witten — Zero-Dimensional Seiberg–Witten Invariant","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-seiberg-witten","aliases":["58-df-seiberg-witten"],"display":"df-seiberg-witten — Zero-Dimensional Seiberg–Witten Invariant","depends_on":["[[58-df-closed-oriented-smooth-manifold]]","[[../batch03/58-df-chern-class.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-seiberg-witten"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-seiberg-witten</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-seiberg-witten — Zero-Dimensional Seiberg–Witten Invariant"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ec1809e41ec24c81\" href=\"?note=ec1809e41ec24c81\" title=\"58-df-closed-oriented-smooth-manifold\">58-df-closed-oriented-smooth-manifold</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"8ee356c2b76fa7ec\" href=\"?note=8ee356c2b76fa7ec\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-chern-class.md\">../batch03/58-df-chern-class.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"<h1 id=\"df-seiberg-witten-—-Seiberg–Witten-Invariants\">df-seiberg-witten — Seiberg–Witten Invariants</h1>\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(X,\\tau_X,\\mathcal A_X)\">\\((X,\\tau_X,\\mathcal A_X)\\)</span> (closed connected oriented smooth <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"4\">\\(4\\)</span>-manifold with chosen oriented atlas)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak s\">\\(\\mathfrak s\\)</span> (spin<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"^c\">\\(^c\\)</span> structure on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"h\">\\(h\\)</span> (a homology orientation of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H^1(X;\\mathbb R)\\oplus H^{2,+}(X;\\mathbb R)\">\\(H^1(X;\\mathbb R)\\oplus H^{2,+}(X;\\mathbb R)\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"g\">\\(g\\)</span> (Riemannian metric) and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\eta\\in\\Omega^{2,+}(X;i\\mathbb R)\">\\(\\eta\\in\\Omega^{2,+}(X;i\\mathbb R)\\)</span> (perturbation)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal M\">\\(\\mathcal M\\)</span> (gauge-equivalence classes of solutions of the perturbed Seiberg--Witten equations) and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varepsilon:\\mathcal M\\to\\{-1,1\\}\">\\(\\varepsilon:\\mathcal M\\to\\{-1,1\\}\\)</span> (orientation signs)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ClosedOrientedSmoothManifold}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ClosedOrientedSmoothManifold}_S\\)</span> (ambient manifold predicate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SpinCStructure}_S,\\mathrm{SWRegularZeroDatum}_S,\\mathrm{SWCount}_S,\\mathrm{SeibergWittenInvariant}_S,\\mathrm{SeibergWittenExpectedDimension}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{SpinCStructure}_S,\\mathrm{SWRegularZeroDatum}_S,\\mathrm{SWCount}_S,\\mathrm{SeibergWittenInvariant}_S,\\mathrm{SeibergWittenExpectedDimension}_S\\)</span> (predicates defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}spin}^{c}\\text{-structure} \\vdash \\mathrm{SpinCStructure}_S(\\mathfrak s,X)\\leftrightarrow \\mathfrak s\\in\\operatorname{Spin}^{c}(X)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}spin}^{c}\\text{-structure} \\vdash \\mathrm{SpinCStructure}_S(\\mathfrak s,X)\\leftrightarrow \\mathfrak s\\in\\operatorname{Spin}^{c}(X)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}seiberg\\text{-}witten\\text{-}dimension} \\vdash \\mathrm{SeibergWittenExpectedDimension}_S(d,X,\\tau_X,\\mathcal A_X,\\mathfrak s)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{ClosedOrientedSmoothManifold}_S(X,\\tau_X,\\mathcal A_X,4)\\land\\mathrm{SpinCStructure}_S(\\mathfrak s,X)\\land d\\in\\mathbb Z\\land4d=c_1(\\mathfrak s)^2-\\bigl(2\\chi(X)+3\\sigma(X)\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}seiberg\\text{-}witten\\text{-}dimension} \\vdash \\mathrm{SeibergWittenExpectedDimension}_S(d,X,\\tau_X,\\mathcal A_X,\\mathfrak s)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{ClosedOrientedSmoothManifold}_S(X,\\tau_X,\\mathcal A_X,4)\\land\\mathrm{SpinCStructure}_S(\\mathfrak s,X)\\land d\\in\\mathbb Z\\land4d=c_1(\\mathfrak s)^2-\\bigl(2\\chi(X)+3\\sigma(X)\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}seiberg\\text{-}witten\\text{-}regular\\text{-}datum} \\vdash \\mathrm{SWRegularZeroDatum}_S(\\mathcal M,\\varepsilon,X,\\tau_X,\\mathcal A_X,\\mathfrak s,h,g,\\eta)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{ClosedOrientedSmoothManifold}_S(X,\\tau_X,\\mathcal A_X,4)\\land\\mathrm{SpinCStructure}_S(\\mathfrak s,X)\\land h\\in\\operatorname{Or}\\bigl(H^1(X;\\mathbb R)\\oplus H^{2,+}(X;\\mathbb R)\\bigr)\\land g\\in\\operatorname{Met}(X)\\land\\eta\\in\\Omega^{2,+}(X;i\\mathbb R)\\land\\mathcal M=\\{[B,\\Psi]_{\\mathcal G_{\\mathfrak s}}:\\operatorname{SW}_{\\mathfrak s,g,\\eta}(B,\\Psi)=0\\}\\land|\\mathcal M|&lt;\\omega\\land\\forall p\\in\\mathcal M\\;(\\operatorname{coker}D^{\\operatorname{SW}}_{p,g,\\eta}=\\{0\\})\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\varepsilon,\\mathcal M,\\{-1,1\\})\\land\\forall p\\in\\mathcal M\\;\\bigl(\\varepsilon(p)=\\operatorname{or}_{\\mathfrak s,g,\\eta,h}(p)\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}seiberg\\text{-}witten\\text{-}regular\\text{-}datum} \\vdash \\mathrm{SWRegularZeroDatum}_S(\\mathcal M,\\varepsilon,X,\\tau_X,\\mathcal A_X,\\mathfrak s,h,g,\\eta)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{ClosedOrientedSmoothManifold}_S(X,\\tau_X,\\mathcal A_X,4)\\land\\mathrm{SpinCStructure}_S(\\mathfrak s,X)\\land h\\in\\operatorname{Or}\\bigl(H^1(X;\\mathbb R)\\oplus H^{2,+}(X;\\mathbb R)\\bigr)\\land g\\in\\operatorname{Met}(X)\\land\\eta\\in\\Omega^{2,+}(X;i\\mathbb R)\\land\\mathcal M=\\{[B,\\Psi]_{\\mathcal G_{\\mathfrak s}}:\\operatorname{SW}_{\\mathfrak s,g,\\eta}(B,\\Psi)=0\\}\\land|\\mathcal M|&lt;\\omega\\land\\forall p\\in\\mathcal M\\;(\\operatorname{coker}D^{\\operatorname{SW}}_{p,g,\\eta}=\\{0\\})\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\varepsilon,\\mathcal M,\\{-1,1\\})\\land\\forall p\\in\\mathcal M\\;\\bigl(\\varepsilon(p)=\\operatorname{or}_{\\mathfrak s,g,\\eta,h}(p)\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}seiberg\\text{-}witten\\text{-}count} \\vdash \\mathrm{SWCount}_S(n,X,\\tau_X,\\mathcal A_X,\\mathfrak s,h,g,\\eta,\\mathcal M,\\varepsilon)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{SeibergWittenExpectedDimension}_S(0,X,\\tau_X,\\mathcal A_X,\\mathfrak s)\\land\\mathrm{SWRegularZeroDatum}_S(\\mathcal M,\\varepsilon,X,\\tau_X,\\mathcal A_X,\\mathfrak s,h,g,\\eta)\\land n=\\sum_{p\\in\\mathcal M}\\varepsilon(p)\\in\\mathbb Z\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}seiberg\\text{-}witten\\text{-}count} \\vdash \\mathrm{SWCount}_S(n,X,\\tau_X,\\mathcal A_X,\\mathfrak s,h,g,\\eta,\\mathcal M,\\varepsilon)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{SeibergWittenExpectedDimension}_S(0,X,\\tau_X,\\mathcal A_X,\\mathfrak s)\\land\\mathrm{SWRegularZeroDatum}_S(\\mathcal M,\\varepsilon,X,\\tau_X,\\mathcal A_X,\\mathfrak s,h,g,\\eta)\\land n=\\sum_{p\\in\\mathcal M}\\varepsilon(p)\\in\\mathbb Z\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}seiberg\\text{-}witten} \\vdash \\mathrm{SeibergWittenInvariant}_S(n,X,\\tau_X,\\mathcal A_X,\\mathfrak s,h)\\leftrightarrow b_2^+(X)&gt;1\\land\\exists g,\\eta,\\mathcal M,\\varepsilon\\;\\mathrm{SWCount}_S(n,X,\\tau_X,\\mathcal A_X,\\mathfrak s,h,g,\\eta,\\mathcal M,\\varepsilon)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}seiberg\\text{-}witten} \\vdash \\mathrm{SeibergWittenInvariant}_S(n,X,\\tau_X,\\mathcal A_X,\\mathfrak s,h)\\leftrightarrow b_2^+(X)&gt;1\\land\\exists g,\\eta,\\mathcal M,\\varepsilon\\;\\mathrm{SWCount}_S(n,X,\\tau_X,\\mathcal A_X,\\mathfrak s,h,g,\\eta,\\mathcal M,\\varepsilon)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This atom covers the zero-dimensional signed-count convention. Positive expected dimension requires insertions and is not identified with a raw cardinality.</li>\n<li>The hypothesis <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"b_2^+(X)&gt;1\">\\(b_2^+(X)&gt;1\\)</span> avoids chamber dependence; metric/perturbation independence is a theorem about the count, not part of its construction.</li>\n<li>The moduli set, regularity condition, homology orientation, and sign function are explicit data; no undeclared “generic” predicate or hidden global moduli symbol remains.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"df-seiberg-witten-—-Seiberg–Witten-Invariants","text":"df-seiberg-witten — Seiberg–Witten Invariants","level":1},{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-closed-oriented-smooth-manifold","status":"resolved","id":"ec1809e41ec24c81","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading